          "filename": "Drought in the wetlands of the Coorong National Park.jpg",
          "caption": "Aftermath of the drought affecting Australia. This wetlands is usually full of water as evidenced by the green reeds and usually is teeming with birdlife like Ibis, Spoonbills, Black swans, Cape Barren Geese and Ducks. Due to the ongoing drought in Australia and the Murray River basin and lack of rain this wetlands has dried up. The birds have gone. This wetlands is in the Coorong National Park.",
